{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"**Block merge.** The PR lets some malformed session expirations through, raises on null expiration, and introduces several ways for the retry worker to stop processing jobs. I inspected all five files and confirmed that the patch reverse-applies in check-only mode against the supplied source and tests. No files were created or modified.\n\n## Merge blockers\n\n| Finding | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| **Null expiration raises instead of being rejected.** The type now allows `null`, but validation calls `.trim()` unconditionally. Other non-string values without a callable `.trim()` also raise. `buildAuthContext` propagates the exception. | [src/auth_client.ts:4](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts:4), [src/auth_client.ts:21](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts:21), [src/auth_client.ts:33](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts:33) |\n| **Unparseable expiration strings pass validation.** `Date.parse` returns `NaN` for an unparseable string, including an empty string after trimming. The patch removes the `NaN` check, so the comparison is false and validation returns `true`. | [pr_diff.patch:18](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch:18), [src/auth_client.ts:22](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts:22) |\n| **Every batch depends on a developer-local staging key.** The worker reads `/Users/dev/keys/staging.pem` before querying the queue, with no configuration exposed through `process_retry_batch`. A missing or unreadable file aborts even an empty batch. The loader also strips bytes from the documented raw HMAC key and accepts an empty result. | [src/retry_worker.py:10](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py:10), [src/retry_worker.py:16](<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py:16), [src/retry_worker.py: